This directory is a modified copy of zune-jpegxl 0.5.2
(https://crates.io/crates/zune-jpegxl/0.5.2, upstream
https://github.com/etemesi254/zune-image/tree/dev/crates/zune-jpegxl,
commit a019244c4a8a4eb713e85fa77f9e18f841d6271b), by Caleb Etemesi,
licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0 OR Zlib (LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE,
LICENSE-ZLIB). quikscope uses it, and distributes this modified copy,
under the Zlib licence option (LICENSE-ZLIB); the MIT and Apache-2.0
texts are kept as they came with the original. As the Zlib licence
requires, this copy is marked as altered (the changes are listed below)
and its licence notices are kept unchanged.

It is compiled as a private module of quikscope (src/media/anim/jxl.rs
includes src/lib.rs with #[path]) rather than as its own crate, so that
quikscope can still be packaged and installed from crates.io. Hence there is
no Cargo.toml here; it depends on zune-core 0.5 through quikscope.

Changes from upstream:

- Animation (src/encoder.rs): `JxlAnimation` and `JxlFrame` plus
  `JxlSimpleEncoder::encode_frame`, which writes one frame of an animated
  codestream. The first frame's image header carries the extra fields with
  an AnimationHeader (ticks per second, loop count) and default tone
  mapping; every frame header carries its duration, frames other than the
  last are saved as reference frame 1, and a frame may cover only part of
  the canvas (custom size and origin), replacing that region of reference
  frame 1. The bit layout follows the JPEG XL codestream specification as
  parsed by jxl-oxide (jxl-image ImageMetadata/AnimationHeader, jxl-frame
  FrameHeader). The still-image path (`encode`) writes what it did before.
- Threads: images with several groups are coded by a fixed number of
  worker threads that take groups from a shared counter, instead of one
  thread per group with the caller spinning while too many were running.
  The no_std build path is gone.
- Module form: `crate::` paths became `super::`, the crate-level
  attributes, `extern crate` lines, std/threads feature gates, trace
  logging and the doc examples (which named the crate) were removed.
